      "source": [
        "## 4. Train one admission classifier per snapshot time\n",
        "\n",
        "Each model is an XGBoost classifier trained on a balanced set and recalibrated (sigmoid) on the calibration window. The features excluded from training and the ordinal mappings are defined in `analysis.py`.\n",
        "\n",
        "`run_analysis` does the rest of the pipeline in one call:\n",
        "\n",
        "- trains the models (`train_models`);\n",
        "- for every test day and snapshot time, turns the per-patient admission probabilities into a distribution over *how many* patients in the ED will be admitted (`predict_bed_counts`);\n",
        "- predicts the patients yet to arrive on the example day and combines both sources (`predict_yet_to_arrive`, `combine_demand`).\n",
        "\n",
        "The figures below are the same ones `make_figures.py` saves."
      ]
